<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
        Exactly the three permissions CLAUDE.md rule 7 allows, and no others.
        Each is here because a specific SDK needs it — none is speculative.

        INTERNET + ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE : AdMob. The ads SDK cannot fetch an ad
            without them, and it checks connectivity before trying.
        BILLING                         : Play Billing, for the one-time unlock.

        Still NOT here, and never will be: storage, camera, location, contacts.
        Sharing a plan and exporting a PDF both use FileProvider into the app's
        own cache.

        ⚠️ THE BUILT APK CONTAINS MORE THAN THESE THREE. Manifest merger pulls in
        further permissions from the ads and Firebase SDKs. Verified by dumping
        the release APK rather than by reading this file:

            com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID      AdMob, Android 13+
            android.permission.ACCESS_ADSERVICES_AD_ID   Privacy Sandbox
            android.permission.ACCESS_ADSERVICES_ATTRIBUTION
            android.permission.ACCESS_ADSERVICES_TOPICS
            android.permission.WAKE_LOCK                 GMS
            android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE        GMS

        These are not declared here and cannot be avoided while using AdMob. Two
        consequences worth knowing:

        1. 🔴 AD_ID must be declared on the Play data safety form. AdMob collects
           the advertising ID, and the privacy policy already says so.
        2. FOREGROUND_SERVICE and WAKE_LOCK sit awkwardly beside NFR-10 ("no
           background work at all"). The app itself starts none — they arrive
           with GMS. Do not add code that uses them.

        TRD §5 says to treat an unexpected permission as a bug. These were
        checked, understood and are expected; anything BEYOND this list is not.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE" />
    <uses-permission android:name="com.android.vending.BILLING" />

    <application
        android:name=".StockCutApplication"
        android:allowBackup="true"
        android:dataExtractionRules="@xml/data_extraction_rules"
        android:fullBackupContent="@xml/backup_rules"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
        android:label="@string/app_name"
        android:roundIcon="@mipmap/ic_launcher_round"
        android:supportsRtl="true"
        android:theme="@style/Theme.StockCut">

        <!--
            AdMob App ID. The value comes from a manifest placeholder that
            defaults to Google's TEST app ID; the real one requires an explicit
            build flag (see app/build.gradle.kts). Clicking a live ad in your own
            app terminates the account, so the safe value is the default.
        -->
        <meta-data
            android:name="com.google.android.gms.ads.APPLICATION_ID"
            android:value="${admobAppId}" />

        <activity
            android:name=".MainActivity"
            android:exported="true"
            android:label="@string/app_name"
            android:theme="@style/Theme.StockCut"
            android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>
        <!--
            Sharing a cut plan as an image, with NO storage permission.
            exported=false and grantUriPermissions mean only the app the user
            picks in the share sheet gets read access, and only to that one file.
        -->
        <provider
            android:name="androidx.core.content.FileProvider"
            android:authorities="${applicationId}.fileprovider"
            android:exported="false"
            android:grantUriPermissions="true">
            <meta-data
                android:name="android.support.FILE_PROVIDER_PATHS"
                android:resource="@xml/file_paths" />
        </provider>

    </application>

</manifest>
